Let counter be 1.
Let output be empty.
Ask for stoppoint with the message When should the programm stop.
Define devidable that takes number,
    If the value of counter remainder number is equal to 0,
        Return 1.
    Otherwise,
        Return 0.
    End if.
End define.
Create a dictionary called combinations.
Let finished be 0.
Set the entry 3 in combinations to Fizz.
Set the entry 5 in combinations to Buzz.
While the value of finished is not equal to 1,
    Ask for go on with the message Type 1 for skipping combination adding and 2 to add a combination.
    If the value of go on is equal to 1,
        Set finished to 1.
    Otherwise,
        Ask for addnum with the message Which number do you want to Add.
        Ask for addword with the message Which word should the numbre have.
        Set the entry the value of addnum in combinations to the value of addword.
    End if.
End while.
While the value of counter is less than or equal to the value of stoppoint,
    For each num and word in combinations,
        Call devidable with the number of num and store the result in result.
        If the value of result is equal to 1,
            Set output to the value of output plus the value of word.
        End if.
    End for each.
    If the value of output is empty,
        Set output to the value of counter.
    End if.
    Say the value of output.
    Set output to empty.
    Add 1 to counter.
End while.
